{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit","id":1439614,"title":"Improved Oath of the Moon: Encourage Balance, Not Spirit","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-13T01:24:10-08:00","id":1439614,"title":"Improved Oath of the Moon: Encourage Balance, Not Spirit","content":"EDIT: I can't change the thread title, but it should have been &quot;Encourage Balance, Not <i>Flesh</i>&quot;<br /> <br /> ...there is some silliness with the Oath of the Moon as written, like eating human flesh being a Breaking Point toward Flesh and Spirit simultaneously. The more I looked at this, the more I realized that it doesn't make sense for violating the Oath of the Moon to always break you toward Spirit. If anything, it should encourage you to stay in balance, right? Why would the Uratha follow an oath that pushes them to one of the extremes? So rather than the Oath encouraging you to become more human-like, I've made it so the various tenets are breaking points in different directions, ultimately encouraging <i>balance</i>.<br /> <br /> <b>THE WOLF MUST HUNT</b>: Violating this tenet is a breaking point toward <b>Flesh</b><i>.</i> This replaces the breaking point &quot;Refusing to participate in the <i>Siskur-Dah&quot; </i>since they're basically the same thing.<br /> <br /> <b>THE PEOPLE DO NOT MURDER THE PEOPLE</b>: Violating this tenet is a breaking point toward <b>Spirit.</b><br /> <br /> <b>THE LOW HONOR THE HIGH; THE HIGH RESPECT THE LOW: </b>Violating this tenet is a breaking point toward <b>Flesh</b><i>.</i><br /> <br /> <b>RESPECT YOUR PREY: </b>Violating this tenet is a breaking point toward <b>Flesh</b><i>.</i><br /> <br /> <b>DO NOT EAT THE FLESH OF MAN OR WOLF: </b>Violating this tenet is a breaking point toward <b>Spirit</b><i>.</i> This replaces the breaking point &quot;Eating human or wolf flesh for Essence<i>&quot; </i>since they're basically the same thing. It still incurs the -3 penalty on the roll instead of the -2 for other Oath violations.<br /> <br /> <b>THE HERD MUST NOT KNOW: </b>Violating this tenet is a breaking point toward <b>Flesh</b>.<br /> <br /> <b>THE URATHA SHALL CLEAVE TO THE HUMAN: </b>Violating this tenet is a breaking point toward <b>Spirit</b>.<br /> <br /> Thus, following the Oath to the letter won't necessarily make you more like a human. It will make you more like a <i>werewolf</i>, encouraging balanced Harmony and removing redundant breaking points that honestly feel like silly oversights. The old 1E Oath of the Moon existed to keep Harmony high back when having high Harmony was desirable. Now that it is not, it seems much more in the spirit of 2E for the Oath to push you to the middle.<br /> <br /> Feel free to adopt or adapt for your own chronicles and let me know how it goes!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4953,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","user":"AsaTJ","date":". 03-13-2021, 11:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:12:56-08:00","id":1439661,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit#post1439614\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...there is some silliness with the Oath of the Moon as written, like eating human flesh being a Breaking Point toward Flesh and Spirit simultaneously. The more I looked at this, the more I realized that it doesn't make sense for violating the Oath of the Moon to always break you toward Spirit. If anything, it should encourage you to stay in balance, right? Why would the Uratha follow an oath that pushes them to one of the extremes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because living in the Flesh and not partaking of spiritually-relevant activity destabilizes you in a way that makes you operate like a movie werewolf, and stopping that from happening more easily is the main benefit of being a werewolf with a Tribe; it <i>doesn't</i> push you to one of the extremes, it pushes you toward the middle <i>of a scale that you start out heavily weighted toward one end of</i>.<br /> <br /> The framework the Forsaken inhabit makes needing to spend time and effort <i>not</i> to change shape to an appropriate form in certain contexts (and keep your stuff while you're doing it) a more attractive proposition than needing to spend Essence and/or take a turn to shift naked, particularly when the subsidiary Bans are just one/two/three among a set you're already managing from belonging to a pack, maintaining territorial rites, and dealing with the occasional bout of bad luck with a Facet. You're a shapeshifting demigod of the hunt that's playing sanitation worker for the cluttered wilderness beyond the veil, and that requires taking a certain amount of time off from acting like a human.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T08:31:59-08:00","id":1439668,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1439661#post1439661\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because living in the Flesh and not partaking of spiritually-relevant activity destabilizes you in a way that makes you operate like a movie werewolf, and stopping that from happening more easily is the main benefit of being a werewolf with a Tribe; it <i>doesn't</i> push you to one of the extremes, it pushes you toward the middle <i>of a scale that you start out heavily weighted toward one end of</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sue that tracks. If you're following the oath faithfully, you will stay on the higher side of Harmony, generally. Unless you're saying that the benefit of having a tribe is that you have the opportunity to <i>violate</i> the Oath, and roll more breaking points toward Spirit. (I realize I worded the thread title poorly and it was too late to edit it - what I meant to say is that the Oath as written in the corebook encourages you toward Flesh.) In which case you're saying the main benefit of a tribe is having more rules that can be broken, to your benefit, which doesn't seem right. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T11:12:01-08:00","id":1439688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1439668#post1439668\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sue that tracks. If you're following the oath faithfully, you will stay on the higher side of Harmony, generally. Unless you're saying that the benefit of having a tribe is that you have the opportunity to <i>violate</i> the Oath, and roll more breaking points toward Spirit. (I realize I worded the thread title poorly and it was too late to edit it - what I meant to say is that the Oath as written in the corebook encourages you toward Flesh.) In which case you're saying the main benefit of a tribe is having more rules that can be broken, to your benefit, which doesn't seem right.</div> </div> </div> </div>The main benefit of having a tribe is that you are a werewolf who actually interacts with the Shadow and has a support structure that allows them to do so regularly and otherwise prevent breaking points toward flesh.<br /> <br /> The Oath is not the whole of Harmony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T12:40:44-08:00","id":1439701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1439688#post1439688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main benefit of having a tribe is that you are a werewolf who actually interacts with the Shadow and has a support structure that allows them to do so regularly and otherwise prevent breaking points toward flesh.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>cocks my head to the side</i><br /> <br /> I'm not sure what you're trying to argue here. That having a tribe is supposed to prevent you from getting &quot;stuck&quot; at high Harmony? But for that to work, you have to <i>violate </i>the Oath of the Moon, which is exactly what the tribes don't want you to do. The logic just doesn't track for me. If the Oath of the Moon always gives you breaking points toward Spirit, then werewolves who actually follow it, and don't go out of their way to break it, would generally stay at higher Harmony.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4953-asatj","name":"AsaTJ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4953_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T13:35:21-08:00","id":1439713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AsaTJ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1439701#post1439701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for that to work, you have to <i>violate </i>the Oath of the Moon</div> </div> </div> </div>Read the last sentence of my post.<br /> <br /> Spending time in the Shadow, participating in or leading the Sacred Hunt, and killing people while you're in a state to remember it will gradually shift a werewolf toward spirit and away from flesh without necessarily destabilizing them. These things have the advantage of being both voluntary and not against the Oath. They are also SOP for most Forsaken and Pure packs. It's more practical to disappear from the mortal world for days at a time when you have the backing of a group of like-minded hunters who don't expect you to live a whole-ass double life as a chronic berserker cannibal.<br /> <br /> Violating the Oath you swear to join a spirit-backed tribal society brings you further out of alignment with your spiritual nature. That this doubles up the breaking points for eating human flesh is a further incentive against doing it (in contrast to the one-way risk a Ghost Wolf takes), because each roll has separate chances of failure and the one that unbalances you further is usually more likely to fail due to the way Harmony affects your breaking point rolls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-13T17:10:03-08:00","id":1439744,"title":"","content":"You had it right the first time, violating the Oath is a breaking point toward Flesh so following it maintains your Spirit-ness.<br /> <br /> That aside, I can\u2019t think of any way in which the houserule itself doesn\u2019t make a lot of sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-16T11:54:46-07:00","id":1444243,"title":"","content":"In addition to the point changes on the scale, there are some serious consequences for committing some acts. Cannibalism, for example, might be a breaking point towards Spirit for a starting werewolf which is balanced towards flesh, but according to the book, acts of cannibalism are extreme violations of the oath which warrant the amputation of a limb with silver, or exile from one's pack and/or tribe (most prefer the amputation). Does this also apply to eating flesh by accident in Kuruth, or when eating an enemy werewolf to cause aggravated damage? <br /> <br /> Regarding The herd must not know, I would imagine that, in a big city like New York or Tokyo, the Uratha are one Kuruth away from exposing themselves to the human race given how much chaos a raging Uratha would cause, especially in this age of mobile devices.<br /> <br /> Regarding the people must not murder the people, that becomes difficult when facing the Pure. If you cannot kill them, but they can kill you (as they did not take the oath), that would put the forsaken at a serious disadvantage. I wonder if it is simpler to just get your non-Uratha packmates loaded with silver buckshot to do the killing instead so as to not cause any violations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T18:43:39-07:00","id":1444584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1444243#post1444243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Regarding The herd must not know, I would imagine that, in a big city like New York or Tokyo, the Uratha are one Kuruth away from exposing themselves to the human race given how much chaos a raging Uratha would cause, especially in this age of mobile devices.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Oath of the Moon has its rhetoric, but given Integrity breaking points I think it's fair to say that the Uratha are in no real danger of widespread exposure. For the most part, people don't want to know that werewolves exist.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Regarding the people must not murder the people, that becomes difficult when facing the Pure. If you cannot kill them, but they can kill you (as they did not take the oath), that would put the forsaken at a serious disadvantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>The book talks about the fact that the Tribes of the Moon heavily debating that tenet (which also has significance for how they relate to one another; packs of Forsaken can have cause to fight each other to the death). The exact interpretation is going to vary between packs and individuals, which can create further complications for how they relate to one another when one group thinks they were in the right and another thinks they're Oathbreakers.<br /> <br /> It all rests on the specifics of what qualifies as murder, rather than rightful killing.<br /> <br /> And apparently, even without swearing the Oath there are Pure who think it's crossing a line to kill their estranged cousins (even if captivity and torture are fair game).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>maryshelly</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wonder if it is simpler to just get your non-Uratha packmates loaded with silver buckshot to do the killing instead so as to not cause any violations.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pretty sure werewolves would consider that a violation in spirit, and just generally disgraceful conduct aside. The Wolf Must Hunt, not hide behind mortals fighting on their behalf. And I don't expect anybody is going to be fooled by technicalities related to who precisely is carrying the silver weapon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-18T21:34:12-07:00","id":1444596,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1444584#post1444584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And apparently, even without swearing the Oath there are Pure who think it's crossing a line to kill their estranged cousins (even if captivity and torture are fair game).</div> </div> </div> </div>They swear a functionally-identical Oath, with their tribal bans serving as extra tenets just like the Forsaken's do for the Oath of the Moon.<br /> <br /> Worth remembering that for all the cannibalism that goes on in it, the Shadow incentivizes leaving your defeated enemies alive to serve as appendages of your greater hunger; take note that the Pure Tribe most concerned with getting converts is the one concerned with respect for the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T18:29:51-07:00","id":1444740,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1444596#post1444596\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They swear a functionally-identical Oath, with their tribal bans serving as extra tenets just like the Forsaken's do for the Oath of the Moon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Iiiinteresting. So is it kind of a case of not so much what you swear but to whom you swear it? That in many respects the Pure would be doing work pleasing to Luna, but for the rejection of having her spirits affirm their Renown and living in accordance with her Auspices?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Worth remembering that for all the cannibalism that goes on in it, the Shadow incentivizes leaving your defeated enemies alive to serve as appendages of your greater hunger; take note that the Pure Tribe most concerned with getting converts is the one concerned with respect for the Shadow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is the tribal ban of the Predator Kings different in this Edition?<br /> <br /> In any case, the implications of the werewolves having an enemy faction who are not only very similar to them but themselves capable of debating the ethics of killing their fellows would be quite fascinating.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T19:02:53-07:00","id":1444743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1444740#post1444740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Iiiinteresting. So is it kind of a case of not so much what you swear but to whom you swear it? That in many respects the Pure would be doing work pleasing to Luna, but for the rejection of having her spirits affirm their Renown and living in accordance with her Auspices?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Pure are mostly doing the Seers thing of mixing their own ambitions for their territory with much more overt and controlling oversight from powerful supernatural beings, and while Luna is more invested in werewolves than Wolf ever was she's still pretty laissez-faire about her Flesh-born progeny, but yes, the operative distinction is between werewolves who're integrated into a spiritually-backed societal framework and werewolves who aren't rather than what powerful spirit that integration was facilitated by.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Is the tribal ban of the Predator Kings different in this Edition? </div> </div> </div>No, I'm describing the Fire-Touched. The Predator Kings fall in the middle of the Pure's axis of What Do We Do With The Forsaken that the other two tribes comprise the opposite views of.<br /> <br /> The Pure Tribes' sacred prey are a lot more open-ended than the Forsaken's, to the point where they can pretty easily justify turning the Sacred Hunt on themselves as well as the Forsaken; the Ivory Claws hunt those who dishonor their family, the Predator Kings hunt those who besmirch the hunt, and the Fire-Touched hunt those who disrespect the Shadow. Replacing their Auspice with a shard of the hateful Essence of a Pure Firstborn tilts this relative freedom to point the knife in certain directions, but the Pure Tribes' sense of spiritual balance largely works the same as their opposite numbers' do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-19T19:55:00-07:00","id":1444750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1444740#post1444740\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Iiiinteresting. So is it kind of a case of not so much what you swear but to whom you swear it? That in many respects the Pure would be doing work pleasing to Luna, but for the rejection of having her spirits affirm their Renown and living in accordance with her Auspices?</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth noting that the Oath of the Moon/Urfarah is less an Oath in the way it would apply for, say, Tribal Oaths, and more descriptor of some of the key factors that affect Uratha. Both Oaths have a functional &quot;The People Do Not Murder the People&quot; because the children of Wolf and Moon risk Harmony in doing so, not because both sides felt such an element in their respective Oaths was in their interests.<br /> <br /> This does not hold with Tribal Oaths/Bans and increasingly smaller forms, obviously.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T00:33:20-07:00","id":1444792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1444743#post1444743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, I'm describing the Fire-Touched.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh no I got that. It just made me wonder how effectively the Predator Kinds integrate among normal people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-20T02:38:56-07:00","id":1444807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1444792#post1444792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh no I got that. It just made me wonder how effectively the Predator Kinds integrate among normal people.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends what you mean by \u201cnormal people\u201d. If you mean humans, the answer is usually \u2018not well\u2019. There are exceptions, but most PKs have little interest in hanging out with humans.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T16:48:21-07:00","id":1445158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1444807#post1444807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Depends what you mean by \u201cnormal people\u201d. If you mean humans, the answer is usually \u2018not well\u2019. There are exceptions, but most PKs have little interest in hanging out with humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right, so the Ban to the best of my understanding in First Edition is that they're forbidden from using things that humans have made. I expect that this would be a severe obstacle to so much as living in a modern city, even without them looking to socialize with people. Would that still be their Ban, or is it possible to interpret the Ban in more accommodating ways, or is it just that sometimes you're going to have some repeatedly breaking the Ban by necessity and needing to make amends for that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-21T17:58:07-07:00","id":1445164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1445158#post1445158\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">is it just that sometimes you're going to have some repeatedly breaking the Ban by necessity and needing to make amends for that.</div> </div> </div> </div>This, though less by necessity and more by want. In Shunned by the Moon, for instance, the example Predator King is a Resources 5 party girl with Status (High Society). She stands out as an example for the Predator Kings, and knows what she's doing is against their tenet, but believes it's helping enough to offset that, and some of the elders are on the fence about it (though it helps that if she screws up, it's her hide and not theirs). But there are plenty of people who eschew modern human conveniences or just don't care enough about them to use them. The fact that werewolves have so many abilities to compensate for the lack of technology, or just shut down technology when necessary, doesn't make it that hard. While we take fridges and microwaves for granted, we also can't turn into predatory animals that can then eat other animals raw. Some people (in real life) have taken the oath to an extreme to believe that they cannot even set foot on roads but that's a bit of an overly exaggerated reading, to me but you may actually have extremists in the setting that believe in it as well. On the other side of the Predator Kings in the book is an unknowing Bale Hound that makes its own clothes and eschews pretty much any modernity, using whatever is necessary for the hunt in its expansive territory.<br /> <br /> Even in first edition the Pure have been about sinning first and 'proving' their forgiveness later, they were very big on self flagellation and 'great deeds' to show how pure they were, even if they were completely willing to break their oaths again and again.<br /> <br /> The Forsaken do it, too, like how the Lodge of Garm is straight up about killing other powerful werewolves, but as PCs and with less (arguably) oppressive bans they ideally take theirs more seriously.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-21-2021, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T17:28:29-07:00","id":1445385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/1439614-improved-oath-of-the-moon-encourage-balance-not-spirit?p=1445164#post1445164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This, though less by necessity and more by want. In Shunned by the Moon, for instance, the example Predator King is a Resources 5 party girl with Status (High Society). She stands out as an example for the Predator Kings, and knows what she's doing is against their tenet, but believes it's helping enough to offset that, and some of the elders are on the fence about it (though it helps that if she screws up, it's her hide and not theirs). But there are plenty of people who eschew modern human conveniences or just don't care enough about them to use them. The fact that werewolves have so many abilities to compensate for the lack of technology, or just shut down technology when necessary, doesn't make it that hard. While we take fridges and microwaves for granted, we also can't turn into predatory animals that can then eat other animals raw. Some people (in real life) have taken the oath to an extreme to believe that they cannot even set foot on roads but that's a bit of an overly exaggerated reading, to me but you may actually have extremists in the setting that believe in it as well. On the other side of the Predator Kings in the book is an unknowing Bale Hound that makes its own clothes and eschews pretty much any modernity, using whatever is necessary for the hunt in its expansive territory.<br /> <br /> Even in first edition the Pure have been about sinning first and 'proving' their forgiveness later, they were very big on self flagellation and 'great deeds' to show how pure they were, even if they were completely willing to break their oaths again and again.<br /> <br /> The Forsaken do it, too, like how the Lodge of Garm is straight up about killing other powerful werewolves, but as PCs and with less (arguably) oppressive bans they ideally take theirs more seriously.</div> </div> </div> </div>Works for me. It all serves to make the Pure more interesting than they might appear at first glance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-22T22:40:27-07:00","id":1445431,"title":"","content":"The ban is the same between 1st and 2nd editions - Honor Nothing of Human Craft - but 2nd edition acknowledges that \u2018smash all technology\u2019 is a simplistic interpretation of the words. Like all Pure tribes in 2e, the tribal oath invites interpretation from the Uratha who follow it. What does it mean to \u201chonor\u201d human craft, just like what does it mean to leave a falsehood unchallenged, or what you accept as lesser purity? For some PKs, using any human-crafted items is off limits. They sew their own clothing (if they wear any) and make their own weapons. Others use technology as long as they don\u2019t care about it. If you need a phone to keep the pack coordinated during a hunt, that\u2019s fine but you don\u2019t care what kind it is - you\u2019re not shopping for the latest iPhone when you can steal an old Nokia off someone. Both do the job you need. Cars are useful for getting from point A to B quickly - one pack steals what they need for transport and then abandons it near the destination. Another owns the cars but takes no care in the dents and scratches they leave in their wake.<br /> <br /> Garima the party animal is running very close to the line, but Dire Wolf doesn\u2019t seem to be offering any thoughts on the matter, and as long as she keeps the other PKs around her convinced that she\u2019s not crossing the line, she gets to keep doing what she does.<br /> <br /> The key thing to remember for the Pure is that it\u2019s the tribe judging what is and isn\u2019t acceptable, and that\u2019s going to vary considerably based on region. What\u2019s acceptable in one location won\u2019t be in another. If you want to shake things up with a Pure game, have a roaming pack of the character\u2019s tribe come to the territory with very different ideas of what is allowed, and let the friction commence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-04-23T02:35:40-07:00","id":1445454,"title":"","content":"I'm suddenly imagining the Pure as the werewolf equivalent to the Amish.<br /> <br /> Specifically in terms of the attitude to modern technology, when and how it is acceptable to use.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}